00:01:47.799 --> 00:01:51.119
specifically our science
courses and new math courses.

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:53.069
I'll start off by talking about science,

00:01:53.069 --> 00:01:54.399
super exciting there.

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:57.379
We have a brand new,
totally redesigned versions

00:01:57.379 --> 00:02:00.459
of several courses, including
high school biology,

00:02:00.459 --> 00:02:03.649
high school physics, AP physics one,

00:02:03.649 --> 00:02:06.569
in addition to that we've
added a lot more new contents

00:02:06.569 --> 00:02:08.699
to our new AP chemistry course

00:02:08.699 --> 00:02:11.179
and very excited about a brand new course

00:02:11.179 --> 00:02:13.879
that we just launched,
AP environmental science.

00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:15.859
Like I said, I'm excited
about all of those things,

00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:17.379
but I wanna talk about two of them

00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:18.919
in a little bit more detail,

00:02:18.919 --> 00:02:22.189
high school biology
and high school, sorry,

00:02:22.189 --> 00:02:25.179
high school biology and
AP environmental science.

00:02:25.179 --> 00:02:27.539
Our high school biology
course it's important to know

00:02:27.539 --> 00:02:30.169
since we had a high school
biology course on Khan Academy

00:02:30.169 --> 00:02:31.669
for the last couple of years,

00:02:31.669 --> 00:02:34.759
this new course is redesigned
from the ground up,

00:02:34.759 --> 00:02:37.759
it's aligned with the next
generation science standards,

00:02:37.759 --> 00:02:40.409
it contains two types
of practice exercises

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:42.519
that are clearly labeled
for the first time ever

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:43.352
on Khan Academy.

00:02:43.352 --> 00:02:47.079
We have exercises that are
called understand exercises,

00:02:47.079 --> 00:02:49.499
and then we have other practice exercises

00:02:49.499 --> 00:02:52.239
called apply exercises.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:54.929
Very exciting to be
able to really delineate

00:02:54.929 --> 00:02:57.789
those two types of
expectations that students

00:02:57.789 --> 00:03:00.679
and teachers can have as
they move through the course.

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:02.789
Also wanna talk about this course

00:03:02.789 --> 00:03:04.229
actually both high school biology

00:03:04.229 --> 00:03:06.449
and AP environmental science showcase

00:03:06.449 --> 00:03:10.609
a fun new aspect of our
courses called lesson teasers.

00:03:10.609 --> 00:03:13.389
These are fun, short little
descriptions of the lessons

00:03:13.389 --> 00:03:15.739
that you can see on the
unit pages for the course,

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:17.379
they're kind of the
Khan Academy equivalent

00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:19.179
of an Easter egg.

00:03:19.179 --> 00:03:21.479
And then when it comes to
AP environmental science,

00:03:21.479 --> 00:03:23.979
this is our first ever AP
environmental science course,

00:03:23.979 --> 00:03:25.989
even though college board has offered that

00:03:25.989 --> 00:03:27.929
for more than 20 years now,

00:03:27.929 --> 00:03:30.639
there was a really big redesign in 2020

00:03:30.639 --> 00:03:32.899
and this course takes that into account.

00:03:32.899 --> 00:03:35.379
So our course was designed by a long time

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:38.329
AP environmental science
teacher, incredibly skilled,

00:03:38.329 --> 00:03:41.759
and also a long time exam
reader so she knows her stuff

00:03:41.759 --> 00:03:45.419
when she was building this
course and it's designed

00:03:45.419 --> 00:03:49.479
to make sure that students
are prepared for that exam.

00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:51.929
And to help with that it's clearly aligned

00:03:51.929 --> 00:03:53.979
to the most up-to-date college board

00:03:53.979 --> 00:03:56.709
AP environmental science
standards and like I said,

00:03:56.709 --> 00:04:00.089
it also has those lesson teasers.

00:04:00.089 --> 00:04:02.019
So also talk a little
bit about math courses.

00:04:02.019 --> 00:04:04.409
We always have a lot of new work

00:04:04.409 --> 00:04:06.089
