00:04:06.089 --> 00:04:09.519
So at this back to school so
just about a month ago in July

00:04:09.519 --> 00:04:11.929
we had major additions to our high school

00:04:11.929 --> 00:04:15.579
and AP statistics courses
and in addition to

00:04:15.579 --> 00:04:17.659
additions in our pre-calculus courses,

00:04:17.659 --> 00:04:21.069
our arithmetic basic
geometry and pre-algebra

00:04:21.069 --> 00:04:22.909
as well as some brand
new get ready courses,

00:04:22.909 --> 00:04:24.329
those have been incredibly popular.

00:04:24.329 --> 00:04:27.239
So we add a new get ready
course for statistics

00:04:27.239 --> 00:04:30.669
and for AP statistics and AP calculus.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:32.699
I'm really excited about the
high school statistics course

00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:36.225
so I'll give like a
little extra blurb there.

00:04:36.225 --> 00:04:39.519
That course is now better aligned
to common core high school

00:04:39.519 --> 00:04:41.709
statistics and probability standards

00:04:41.709 --> 00:04:44.099
and there's new instructional
and practice content

00:04:44.099 --> 00:04:47.029
for standards and new
and interesting topics

00:04:47.029 --> 00:04:49.719
like study design
probability, distributions,

00:04:49.719 --> 00:04:51.549
and expected value.

00:04:51.549 --> 00:04:54.419
And then when it comes to
the videos and exercises,

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:56.649
I'm happy to announce
that now they go beyond

00:04:56.649 --> 00:05:00.449
those sort of route, procedures
and context free data

00:05:00.449 --> 00:05:03.259
that sometimes can make
statistics less interesting.

00:05:03.259 --> 00:05:06.579
So in this course now learners
can both apply concepts

00:05:06.579 --> 00:05:10.239
and procedures in real world contexts,

00:05:10.239 --> 00:05:11.689
can answer questions like,

00:05:11.689 --> 00:05:13.369
should you buy that extended warranty

00:05:13.369 --> 00:05:15.789
that the salesperson
is trying to offer you?

00:05:15.789 --> 00:05:18.069
So I'll leave it at that,

00:05:18.069 --> 00:05:20.949
all altogether there's
just a ton of new content,

00:05:20.949 --> 00:05:23.299
very excited about it and the content team

00:05:23.299 --> 00:05:25.976
has been working really
hard to provide this content

00:05:25.976 --> 00:05:29.429
for these new courses for
students all over the U.S

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:31.029
and eventually around the world.

00:05:32.349 --> 00:05:33.182
- That's awesome.

00:05:33.182 --> 00:05:35.729
And I know I have seen
you and the whole team

00:05:35.729 --> 00:05:39.799
hard at work for a year creating
these courses basically.

00:05:39.799 --> 00:05:42.969
So congratulations on
all of their launches.

00:05:42.969 --> 00:05:45.111
Who do you think about

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.179
when you're designing these courses?

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:48.339
How do you think about
the audience for them

00:05:48.339 --> 00:05:50.039
and who they're built for?

00:05:50.039 --> 00:05:51.169
- Yeah, that's a good question.

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:53.949
And historically Khan
Academy really looks at

00:05:53.949 --> 00:05:56.989
the independent learner and
we're still very focused

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.409
and wanna make sure that
everything we produce

00:05:59.409 --> 00:06:02.609
is great just-in-time
learning for anybody out there

00:06:02.609 --> 00:06:05.609
who just needs a little boost
when it comes to biology

00:06:05.609 --> 00:06:07.469
or pre-calculus or anything else.

00:06:07.469 --> 00:06:09.229
But these courses in particular

00:06:09.229 --> 00:06:11.479
we're designing really
with the classroom in mind.

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:13.839
So really thinking about
the teachers and students

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:16.099
and classroom context, and what can we do

00:06:16.099 --> 00:06:19.229
to help support that
learning best as possible

00:06:19.229 --> 00:06:21.799
while still making sure
that these courses provide

00:06:21.799 --> 00:06:25.429
exceptional value for
anybody who's just coming in

00:06:25.429 --> 00:06:28.512
to learn a concept inside
or outside of the classroom.

00:06:30.039 --> 00:06:32.739
- So what does that look
like then in application

00:06:32.739 --> 00:06:35.729
for it to be really also
thinking about teachers

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:40.216
and what might teachers
see or be responding to

00:06:40.216 --> 00:06:41.602
in the new courses?

00:06:42.599 --> 00:06:44.019
- Yeah, really I think that comes down

00:06:44.019 --> 00:06:45.069
to standards alignment.

00:06:45.069 --> 00:06:48.049
So I mentioned with the science
courses that these are built

00:06:48.049 --> 00:06:50.859
with the next generation
science standards in mind,

00:06:50.859 --> 00:06:53.129
all of our AP courses
are really built with

00:06:53.129 --> 00:06:56.009
the AP standards directly in mind.

00:06:56.009 --> 00:06:58.329
They're built by and reviewed by teachers

00:06:58.329 --> 00:07:00.809
in classrooms teaching these subjects.

00:07:00.809 --> 00:07:03.729
So all of those components
together we really hope

00:07:03.729 --> 00:07:06.629
that it's gonna supercharge
what's going on in classrooms.

00:07:08.939 --> 00:07:11.819
- So how can people give us feedback

00:07:11.819 --> 00:07:15.119
on whether these new courses
are hitting the mark or not?

00:07:15.119 --> 00:07:17.189
- Yeah, really glad you
asked that question.

00:07:17.189 --> 00:07:20.109
Please everybody out
there give us feedback,

00:07:20.109 --> 00:07:21.789
especially on these science courses,

00:07:21.789 --> 00:07:24.119
this is the first time we're
designing these courses

00:07:24.119 --> 00:07:26.579
in this particular way and you'll notice,

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:28.439
longtime Khan Academy users will notice

