00:08:25.289 --> 00:08:28.699
So yes, I hear you they
are a little short,

00:08:28.699 --> 00:08:31.409
I'm so excited that
somebody has already gone in

00:08:31.409 --> 00:08:34.789
and completed the entire AP
environmental science course.

00:08:34.789 --> 00:08:36.379
So that's great to hear.

00:08:36.379 --> 00:08:37.779
Awesome, I love hearing feedback

00:08:37.779 --> 00:08:40.419
about how people like our courses,

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:43.149
also I would love feedback about
what would you like to see?

00:08:43.149 --> 00:08:46.399
So, yes, these are a little
bit on the short side.

00:08:46.399 --> 00:08:50.269
What would help you have
even a better experience

00:08:50.269 --> 00:08:51.499
in your course?

00:08:51.499 --> 00:08:53.609
Let us know and we'll put that on the list

00:08:53.609 --> 00:08:56.649
of things to add as we continue
to work on these courses

00:08:56.649 --> 00:08:58.319
and release more and more updates

00:08:58.319 --> 00:09:00.362
in the future months and year or so.

00:09:01.429 --> 00:09:03.129
- I'm so impressed that
someone's actually gone through

00:09:03.129 --> 00:09:04.585
the whole course already.

00:09:04.585 --> 00:09:06.027
(Kristen laughs)

00:09:06.027 --> 00:09:07.309
Good for them.

00:09:07.309 --> 00:09:12.309
So as I've poked into some of the courses,

00:09:12.789 --> 00:09:17.789
I know (indistinct) but
there's some new voices here,

00:09:17.909 --> 00:09:19.769
tell me a little more about them.

00:09:19.769 --> 00:09:22.759
- Yeah, there are a lot of
new voices in our videos.

00:09:22.759 --> 00:09:25.279
So yeah, we really had
an intentional effort,

00:09:25.279 --> 00:09:26.829
especially in the science videos

00:09:26.829 --> 00:09:28.929
to bring a more diverse set of voices

00:09:28.929 --> 00:09:31.099
into our video creation process.

00:09:31.099 --> 00:09:34.209
And no fear out there, Sal
is still making videos.

00:09:34.209 --> 00:09:36.849
He's made videos in our
new science content,

00:09:36.849 --> 00:09:39.369
but we've also brought
in more than a dozen

00:09:39.369 --> 00:09:41.619
new video creators.

00:09:41.619 --> 00:09:43.456
This is mostly focused on the high school

00:09:43.456 --> 00:09:45.499
and AP science so far.

00:09:45.499 --> 00:09:47.499
We're also hot in the middle of creating

00:09:47.499 --> 00:09:49.179
middle-school science for the first time,

00:09:49.179 --> 00:09:51.939
so that's a little sneak
preview for folks on Ed Talks

00:09:51.939 --> 00:09:54.399
that middle-school science
content is coming soon,

00:09:54.399 --> 00:09:58.119
and we'll be using those
new video creators,

00:09:58.119 --> 00:10:00.209
and even more new video creators

00:10:00.209 --> 00:10:02.339
in our middle-school
content but like I said,

00:10:02.339 --> 00:10:03.809
Sal is still in the mix

00:10:03.809 --> 00:10:06.022
and is still creating great videos for us.

00:10:07.329 --> 00:10:08.162
- Great.

00:10:08.162 --> 00:10:10.439
Well, I know when I
came on I was fascinated

00:10:10.439 --> 00:10:13.806
by the process of how
these videos get made

00:10:13.806 --> 00:10:15.419
and how involved it is.

00:10:15.419 --> 00:10:18.319
Can you share a little
bit of that with folks?

00:10:18.319 --> 00:10:19.152
- Sure.

00:10:19.152 --> 00:10:21.719
Yeah it is a pretty long process

00:10:21.719 --> 00:10:24.519
and we do that because we care
so much about the content.

00:10:24.519 --> 00:10:26.339
We wanna make sure that
we're providing the best,

00:10:26.339 --> 00:10:29.339
most accurate, most
engaging content possible.

00:10:29.339 --> 00:10:32.779
So when we're talking about
videos what really happens first

00:10:32.779 --> 00:10:35.589
is we have our content
experts that are working

00:10:35.589 --> 00:10:38.529
with Khan Academy will write up a request

00:10:38.529 --> 00:10:40.859
for a new video and inside that request,

00:10:40.859 --> 00:10:44.009
it'll have things like the
standards that that video

00:10:44.009 --> 00:10:45.619
need to be aligned to,

00:10:45.619 --> 00:10:47.979
it'll have any kind of misconceptions

00:10:47.979 --> 00:10:50.399
that we wanna make sure we address.

00:10:50.399 --> 00:10:52.649
It will have any kind of
language that we really

00:10:52.649 --> 00:10:55.139
wanna make sure that students hear

00:10:55.139 --> 00:10:57.099
and may include language
that we wanna make sure

00:10:57.099 --> 00:10:59.669
that students don't quite yet because

00:10:59.669 --> 00:11:01.532
the sequencing of the video is such that

00:11:01.532 --> 00:11:04.579
we want to introduce content and terms

00:11:04.579 --> 00:11:06.259
at certain times during the course

00:11:06.259 --> 00:11:07.859
so it might not quite be ready yet.

00:11:07.859 --> 00:11:09.399
So we take that exercise request,

00:11:09.399 --> 00:11:11.649
we hand it over to a new video creator,

00:11:11.649 --> 00:11:13.949
they create a script,
that script comes back

00:11:13.949 --> 00:11:17.729
to Khan Academy content experts for review

00:11:17.729 --> 00:11:20.389
there's back and forth
with that scripting process

00:11:20.389 --> 00:11:23.549
then the video creator creates
a first draft of a video,

00:11:23.549 --> 00:11:26.449
which then comes back again
to the Khan Academy experts

00:11:26.449 --> 00:11:28.189
and even I get into the
mix a little bit here

00:11:28.189 --> 00:11:30.199
and review that video, make notes,

00:11:30.199 --> 00:11:33.429
send that information back
to the video content creator

00:11:33.429 --> 00:11:35.609
and then that process sort of continues.

00:11:35.609 --> 00:11:37.399
It usually takes two to three drafts

00:11:37.399 --> 00:11:39.849
of the actual video after
the scripting process

00:11:39.849 --> 00:11:41.799
before we're really aligned

00:11:41.799 --> 00:11:44.239
that this video is ready to be published

00:11:44.239 --> 00:11:47.039
and that can take a couple
of weeks sometimes per video.

00:11:48.209 --> 00:11:49.042
- Wow.

00:11:49.042 --> 00:11:52.399
Yeah, I've seen this going back and forth

00:11:52.399 --> 00:11:54.949
then all of the detailed comments

00:11:54.949 --> 00:11:58.839
and the deep discussions
about the content itself

00:11:58.839 --> 00:12:01.259
and what's the right way to present it,

00:12:01.259 --> 00:12:04.149
so congratulations to you and the team

00:12:04.149 --> 00:12:08.059
it's really a lot of work I
