00:21:16.649 --> 00:21:21.649
not surprisingly, learning
science and how we fit those in.

00:21:22.192 --> 00:21:25.789
So help folks who are out there understand

00:21:25.789 --> 00:21:28.099
a little bit more about
how these things work,

00:21:28.099 --> 00:21:32.049
Adam and I, over the past
year, have started a project

00:21:32.049 --> 00:21:35.819
to start thinking about how we make sure

00:21:35.819 --> 00:21:38.499
things like our hints and our rationales

00:21:38.499 --> 00:21:42.029
are aligned to what
education research says

00:21:42.029 --> 00:21:45.899
they should be and how we can
write hints in the best way

00:21:45.899 --> 00:21:49.019
to help students really
get the support they need

00:21:49.019 --> 00:21:51.169
to answer questions.

00:21:51.169 --> 00:21:52.649
But can you just talk a little bit about

00:21:52.649 --> 00:21:56.225
hints and rationales and
why those are important

00:21:56.225 --> 00:21:59.281
in the exercises that we create?

00:21:59.281 --> 00:22:00.645
- Sure, yeah absolutely.

00:22:00.645 --> 00:22:02.319
I can talk about that for much longer

00:22:02.319 --> 00:22:03.959
than we actually have time for

00:22:03.959 --> 00:22:05.589
so I'll try to keep it short.

00:22:05.589 --> 00:22:07.739
But overall the thing that I really love

00:22:07.739 --> 00:22:10.931
about hints and rationales,
these are things that come up

00:22:10.931 --> 00:22:13.569
right on the screen, instant feedback,

00:22:13.569 --> 00:22:15.319
when a student answers a question,

00:22:15.319 --> 00:22:16.799
if they answer the question correctly

00:22:16.799 --> 00:22:19.469
they can still see all of
these rationales and hints

00:22:19.469 --> 00:22:22.149
that come up or if they
answer a question incorrectly,

00:22:22.149 --> 00:22:24.299
they can get a hint
that starts to stepwise

00:22:24.299 --> 00:22:27.009
work them through each
part of the question

00:22:27.009 --> 00:22:30.909
or a rationale which is a
different form of feedback

00:22:30.909 --> 00:22:35.529
that is tagged exactly to
each question answer choice.

00:22:35.529 --> 00:22:38.079
So usually if there's a
question that's more procedural

00:22:38.079 --> 00:22:40.339
where you need to kind of
work through step by step,

00:22:40.339 --> 00:22:42.849
we'll have a hints to help
you work through step by step

00:22:42.849 --> 00:22:45.379
but if the question isn't that
kind of procedural question,

00:22:45.379 --> 00:22:48.499
and it's more conceptual or
more applied then we'll give

00:22:48.499 --> 00:22:52.599
more exact feedback at the
item answer choice level

00:22:52.599 --> 00:22:55.039
and that's called a
rationale but either way

00:22:55.039 --> 00:22:56.039
that you get that feedback

00:22:56.039 --> 00:22:58.049
I think the most important
thing is that students

00:22:58.049 --> 00:23:01.059
can go through questions at their own pace

00:23:01.059 --> 00:23:02.889
as they get things correct and incorrect,

00:23:02.889 --> 00:23:06.129
they can see the rationale
for the correct answer

00:23:06.129 --> 00:23:09.059
or the hints so the way
to get the correct answer

00:23:09.059 --> 00:23:11.869
if they're having trouble and
then even more powerfully,

00:23:11.869 --> 00:23:14.519
they can just go through
the exercise again,

00:23:14.519 --> 00:23:16.069
they'll see slightly different questions

00:23:16.069 --> 00:23:17.419
each time they go through

00:23:17.419 --> 00:23:19.519
and then they'll get a chance
to apply that knowledge

00:23:19.519 --> 00:23:21.249
that maybe they learned in a rationale

00:23:21.249 --> 00:23:24.389
or in a hands to another shot just to see

00:23:24.389 --> 00:23:26.999
if they can solidify that
concept in their mind.

00:23:26.999 --> 00:23:30.369
So I think between getting
that just in time information

00:23:30.369 --> 00:23:31.899
about what's going on in that question

00:23:31.899 --> 00:23:34.599
and then the opportunity
to have that growth mindset

00:23:34.599 --> 00:23:38.599
to persevere and try again
make the practice exercises

00:23:38.599 --> 00:23:40.492
on Khan very powerful.

00:23:42.159 --> 00:23:43.039
- Absolutely.

00:23:43.039 --> 00:23:46.159
And so if you're a student out
there or if you're a teacher

00:23:46.159 --> 00:23:47.949
or a parent coaching a
student and you're thinking,

00:23:47.949 --> 00:23:49.749
should I ask for a hint or not?

00:23:49.749 --> 00:23:52.489
Here's a little tip to walk you through.

00:23:52.489 --> 00:23:55.329
If you're looking at the
question and you think,

00:23:55.329 --> 00:23:58.889
I have no idea how to try
to start to answer this,

00:23:58.889 --> 00:23:59.909
take a hint.

00:23:59.909 --> 00:24:03.809
If you're thinking, I might have an idea,

00:24:03.809 --> 00:24:05.499
go ahead and try that,

00:24:05.499 --> 00:24:07.389
go ahead and work through it on your own

00:24:07.389 --> 00:24:10.169
and actually in the research
shows if you're trying

00:24:10.169 --> 00:24:15.169
to answer a question
and you give it a try,

00:24:15.191 --> 00:24:18.579
that's a good approach to
take before taking a hint

00:24:18.579 --> 00:24:20.909
and then if you don't
get it right go ahead

00:24:20.909 --> 00:24:22.249
and look at the hint.

00:24:22.249 --> 00:24:23.899
Look at all the rationale depending on

00:24:23.899 --> 00:24:26.009
what kind of question it is,

00:24:26.009 --> 00:24:28.829
if it's that procedural
kind of question or not,

00:24:28.829 --> 00:24:30.779
and then keep asking
yourself those questions

00:24:30.779 --> 00:24:33.750
and then take a minute as Adam said

00:24:33.750 --> 00:24:36.129
to really think about that
hint or that rationale

00:24:36.129 --> 00:24:38.929
and maybe explain it to
yourself in your own words

00:24:38.929 --> 00:24:42.479
like why, oh yeah that's the next step

00:24:42.479 --> 00:24:46.379
because I needed to get the
variables all on one side

00:24:46.379 --> 00:24:50.009
or that's the correct answer because,

00:24:50.009 --> 00:24:51.589
say it in your own words,

00:24:51.589 --> 00:24:54.029
that actually really will
help you remember it later.

00:24:54.029 --> 00:24:56.609
So little tip for those that are out there

00:24:56.609 --> 00:24:59.791
learning and thinking about new questions

00:24:59.791 --> 00:25:04.059
and think how to work
through some of our content

00:25:04.059 --> 00:25:05.109
and where things are.

00:25:05.967 --> 00:25:07.069
- Absolutely.

00:25:07.069 --> 00:25:08.989
I'll do a little shout out here

00:25:08.989 --> 00:25:11.789
to some teacher tools because
teachers might be listening.

00:25:11.789 --> 00:25:14.279
And the one thing that I said earlier,

00:25:14.279 --> 00:25:15.659
you can get different questions every time

00:25:15.659 --> 00:25:18.969
you go through, incredibly
powerful to be able to have

00:25:18.969 --> 00:25:20.249
that second chance.

00:25:20.249 --> 00:25:22.579
Also for teachers though
if you want to have

00:25:22.579 --> 00:25:25.759
all of your students answer
exactly the same questions

00:25:25.759 --> 00:25:28.649
so that you can go over those
in class and know exactly

00:25:28.649 --> 00:25:31.609
that every student has seen
each one of those questions,

00:25:31.609 --> 00:25:33.609
you have that option
with our teacher tools

00:25:33.609 --> 00:25:36.229
when you make an assignments
to all of your students

00:25:36.229 --> 00:25:37.799
you can check a little box that says,

00:25:37.799 --> 00:25:39.789
show all of my students
different questions

00:25:39.789 --> 00:25:42.019
or show all of my students
the same questions,

00:25:42.019 --> 00:25:43.679
and that can be really useful

00:25:43.679 --> 00:25:46.469
when you're doing a group
discussion in classrooms

00:25:46.469 --> 00:25:48.509
so that everybody has seen the same things

00:25:48.509 --> 00:25:50.329
and you can go through
those hints and rationales

00:25:50.329 --> 00:25:52.759
as a group as a different way

00:25:52.759 --> 00:25:55.342
to kind of get that learning experience.

00:25:57.069 --> 00:25:58.099
- Great.

00:25:58.099 --> 00:26:00.409
We've got a question
coming in from Facebook,

00:26:00.409 --> 00:26:02.179
David Clever-Camp wants to know,

00:26:02.179 --> 00:26:05.329
how might Khan Academy
be used to facilitate

00:26:05.329 --> 00:26:08.379
support of English language
learners in the future

00:26:08.379 --> 00:26:11.032
or teachers of English
as a second language?

00:26:13.039 --> 00:26:15.392
- Yeah, would you like
me to take that, Kristen?

00:26:15.392 --> 00:26:16.779
(Adam laughs)

00:26:16.779 --> 00:26:17.612
- Go for it.

00:26:18.539 --> 00:26:19.779
- Please chime in.

00:26:19.779 --> 00:26:23.929
So we have our English language
arts courses up right now,

00:26:23.929 --> 00:26:26.178
which is a little bit
different of a question

00:26:26.178 --> 00:26:27.639
that I think you're asking.

00:26:27.639 --> 00:26:29.869
We're working on trying to figure out

00:26:29.869 --> 00:26:32.029
the best ways to be able to support

00:26:32.029 --> 00:26:34.219
English language learners on the site.

00:26:34.219 --> 00:26:35.869
At the moment we're trying to make sure

00:26:35.869 --> 00:26:38.379
that at least all the
content that's been up

00:26:38.379 --> 00:26:39.212
for a little while,

00:26:39.212 --> 00:26:41.519
this is not true for
the new science courses

00:26:41.519 --> 00:26:43.579
that just came out quite
yet, but to make sure that

00:26:43.579 --> 00:26:45.639
all of those are also available in Spanish

00:26:45.639 --> 00:26:47.669
to at least help English language learners

00:26:47.669 --> 00:26:49.389
that are starting from a Spanish base

00:26:49.389 --> 00:26:51.369
so that you can see all of our content

00:26:51.369 --> 00:26:54.149
both in Spanish and in
English quite easily.

00:26:54.149 --> 00:26:56.209
That's our goal, we're not quite there yet

00:26:56.209 --> 00:26:58.099
for some of these new
courses as I mentioned,

00:26:58.099 --> 00:27:01.209
but hopefully that will help
with some of that transition

00:27:01.209 --> 00:27:03.379
along with looking at our ELA

00:27:03.379 --> 00:27:05.239
or English language arts content,

00:27:05.239 --> 00:27:07.239
hopefully at least in the short term

00:27:07.239 --> 00:27:09.069
we'll help learners like that.

00:27:09.069 --> 00:27:12.619
We're also very careful to make
sure that our reading levels

00:27:12.619 --> 00:27:15.849
for each of the grades is
matched to make sure that

00:27:15.849 --> 00:27:18.379
we're keeping reading
levels where they should be

00:27:18.379 --> 00:27:20.239
for sixth grade or seventh graders,

00:27:20.239 --> 00:27:22.659
ninth graders, tenth graders, et cetera.

00:27:22.659 --> 00:27:26.629
So we're also hoping
that that will help folks

00:27:26.629 --> 00:27:28.769
that are learning English while also

00:27:28.769 --> 00:27:30.869
learning science and math on Khan Academy.

00:27:32.489 --> 00:27:33.939
- Great, thank you.

00:27:33.939 --> 00:27:38.529
One more question I'll start
and then you can follow up.

00:27:38.529 --> 00:27:40.496
Mr. New Blocks on YouTube,

00:27:40.496 --> 00:27:44.516
"Any tips on what to do if
you get bored during class?"

00:27:45.969 --> 00:27:49.449
This is obviously a
question that we get a lot

00:27:49.449 --> 00:27:52.579
from both students who
are looking for help

00:27:52.579 --> 00:27:54.809
and then teachers who are
looking to help students

00:27:54.809 --> 00:27:57.769
how to stay motivated and engaged in this.

00:27:57.769 --> 00:28:00.249
And so there's a couple
of things that I'll say

00:28:00.249 --> 00:28:02.679
that I think are important.

00:28:02.679 --> 00:28:07.679
So one is think about how might this apply

00:28:07.729 --> 00:28:10.189
to something that you're interested in.

00:28:10.189 --> 00:28:13.499
So think about, is there
something I can take away here

00:28:13.499 --> 00:28:17.209
that's gonna help me in a
hobby that I'm interested in?

00:28:17.209 --> 00:28:19.735
Is there something that
I can take away here

00:28:19.735 --> 00:28:21.909
that's gonna help me in a
future job that I might like?

00:28:21.909 --> 00:28:24.949
Or is there something here
that just is really interesting

00:28:24.949 --> 00:28:28.709
about how the world works and I can take

00:28:28.709 --> 00:28:31.049
and understand better how something works?

00:28:31.049 --> 00:28:35.219
How my bicycle tires and the me peddling

00:28:35.219 --> 00:28:36.659
helps move those tires.

00:28:36.659 --> 00:28:39.649
There's a whole bunch of
interesting physics behind that.

00:28:39.649 --> 00:28:41.289
But think about, like I said,

00:28:41.289 --> 00:28:43.629
thinking about how the
things you're learning

00:28:43.629 --> 00:28:47.499
are applying to the real world
and are kind of exciting.

00:28:47.499 --> 00:28:49.509
What are the things that
Sal always talks about

00:28:49.509 --> 00:28:54.509
that's amazing is we have
so much collected knowledge

00:28:55.059 --> 00:28:59.219
in our textbooks or in the
videos that we've created

00:28:59.219 --> 00:29:01.464
and the exercises that we're doing

00:29:01.464 --> 00:29:04.256
and what a privilege it is for us to have

00:29:04.256 --> 00:29:05.989
all of this just readily available.

00:29:05.989 --> 00:29:08.099
Think of all of the
people who've contributed

00:29:08.099 --> 00:29:10.552
to all of this knowledge
and where that is,

00:29:11.819 --> 00:29:15.379
can help kind of think
about how exciting it is

00:29:15.379 --> 00:29:18.469
to have the opportunity to
work through some of it.

00:29:18.469 --> 00:29:20.969
So that's some of the big pieces.

00:29:20.969 --> 00:29:23.329
All right, here's a
really specific though,

00:29:23.329 --> 00:29:24.889
kind of more behavioral,

00:29:24.889 --> 00:29:27.349
if you're familiar with
behavioral psychology,

00:29:27.349 --> 00:29:30.409
is have something where you can check in

00:29:30.409 --> 00:29:32.979
every so often you might
set it for five minutes,

00:29:32.979 --> 00:29:34.489
you might set it for 10 minutes.

00:29:34.489 --> 00:29:36.579
It just gives you a reminder
and whenever you see it,

00:29:36.579 --> 00:29:38.129
you think, am I paying attention?

00:29:38.129 --> 00:29:39.289
Am I paying attention?

00:29:39.289 --> 00:29:40.519
Is my mind wandering?

00:29:40.519 --> 00:29:42.039
And that can actually help train you

00:29:42.039 --> 00:29:44.629
to make sure you're
staying paying attention

00:29:44.629 --> 00:29:48.329
and being able to focus better
and help teach you that way.

00:29:48.329 --> 00:29:50.869
So lots of different
things that might help you

00:29:50.869 --> 00:29:52.669
stay focused.

00:29:52.669 --> 00:29:54.769
Adam, any thoughts for you about staying

00:29:54.769 --> 00:29:57.259
and what happens if
you get bored in class?

00:29:57.259 --> 00:29:59.826
- Yeah and I've been there
maybe not so long ago

00:29:59.826 --> 00:30:01.879
and they're bored in class.

00:30:01.879 --> 00:30:03.849
And I really liked the idea of applying

00:30:03.849 --> 00:30:05.579
like I'm thinking about what's going on

00:30:05.579 --> 00:30:09.089
up on the board and the
book, on the video, in class,

00:30:09.089 --> 00:30:12.149
or even on Khan Academy that
can relate to what's going on

00:30:12.149 --> 00:30:14.779
in your life and be more relevant.

00:30:14.779 --> 00:30:18.209
But the spin that I'll
put on that is sometime

00:30:18.209 --> 00:30:19.619
for me it's really
interesting to think about

00:30:19.619 --> 00:30:21.769
connections between courses.

00:30:21.769 --> 00:30:23.689
So if I'm in a chemistry course

00:30:23.689 --> 00:30:25.999
or listening to a chemistry lecture,

00:30:25.999 --> 00:30:28.099
I'm a biologist at heart so I love biology

00:30:28.099 --> 00:30:30.639
and I'm thinking about
how does this chemistry

00:30:30.639 --> 00:30:33.749
that I'm learning relates
to the biology that I love

00:30:33.749 --> 00:30:37.239
or how does this statistical analysis

00:30:37.239 --> 00:30:39.449
that I find really interesting how is that

00:30:39.449 --> 00:30:42.839
being applied, could be
applied to a physics problem,

00:30:42.839 --> 00:30:44.599
even not a specific physics problem

00:30:44.599 --> 00:30:46.909
but a general concept in physics

00:30:46.909 --> 00:30:48.679
how could these two things relate

00:30:48.679 --> 00:30:50.329
and you can kind of play
those games in your mind

00:30:50.329 --> 00:30:53.049
a little bit taking a subject or a topic

00:30:53.049 --> 00:30:53.889
that you're interested in,

00:30:53.889 --> 00:30:57.959
whether it's an academic topic
or something around sports

00:30:57.959 --> 00:31:00.379
or reading, something that you've read

00:31:00.379 --> 00:31:02.479
or some kind of hobby
like Kristen mentioned

00:31:02.479 --> 00:31:05.479
and apply that to the topic at hand

00:31:05.479 --> 00:31:08.382
and that definitely has kept
me interested in the past.

00:31:09.729 --> 00:31:11.029
- Great.

00:31:11.029 --> 00:31:14.619
So one more plug we would
love to hear from you

00:31:14.619 --> 00:31:17.239
about how you find these new courses.

00:31:17.239 --> 00:31:18.479
Please give us feedback.

00:31:18.479 --> 00:31:21.234
Adam is sitting ready to read it.

00:31:21.234 --> 00:31:26.234
So please do take and as you're
going through the courses,

00:31:27.739 --> 00:31:29.379
let us know how you find them

00:31:29.379 --> 00:31:32.749
and what else we can do to
make them better in particular.

00:31:32.749 --> 00:31:35.529
So thank you, Adam for joining us today.

